1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:04,320
School notices can hide the next step
in a wall of unfamiliar words.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:09,520
School Notice Decoder turns a photo
into a plan for multilingual families.

3
00:00:09,520 --> 00:00:12,460
This is a fictional school notice.

4
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:16,840
Tesseract reads the image in the browser,
and the parent can correct the text.

5
00:00:16,840 --> 00:00:21,280
Before optional AI analysis,
the student’s name is masked locally.

6
00:00:21,280 --> 00:00:24,060
The exact outgoing text
remains visible for review.

7
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:29,820
The no-key demo uses a clearly labeled sample engine,
not a live AI response.

8
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:33,640
Here, Spanish instructions
become checkable actions.

9
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,900
Every task links back to its source.

10
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:38,220
Calendar dates stay editable.

11
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:43,420
Only after a parent checks them can an all-day reminder
file be downloaded. No timezone is guessed.

12
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:45,680
Gemini is optional.

13
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:51,100
The prototype allows synthetic, non-sensitive content only,
and explains its free-tier data use.

14
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,900
The goal is not another translation.

15
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:58,100
It is a next step a family can inspect,
understand, and act on.
